nflated\n            #     KV interval AND the clean weight intervals), and the union-merge\n            #     cancels that overlap → the union equals the true H2D engine-busy\n            #     span (validated disjoint vs the nsys copy-engine timeline).\n            #   • weight_load_time is the CLEAN head-of-queue weight union (weight\n            #     is prefetched first, never queued behind KV → never absorbed).\n            # KVLoad = union − weight is then exact, additive by construction\n            # (WLoad+KVLoad = union ≤ GPUFwd), zero schedule perturbation (pure\n            # post-hoc arithmetic on the fast baseline's recorded events), and a\n            # real measurement (a genuine KV slowdown grows the union → the\n            # residual).  Validated: union 150.79 − weight 112.92 = 37.87 ≈ nsys\n            # KV 37.86 @b64.  (Stream-ordering fixes — weight-waits-KV / alias /\n            # KV-waits-weight — were all rejected: they change the schedule and\n            # collapse the depth-2 weight prefetch, +25-31% TPOT.)\n            engine_busy_union = self._merge_union(\n                weight_memcpy_times + kv_memcpy_times)\n            kv_load_time = max(0.0, engine_busy_union - weight_load_time)\n\n        # ── Stall computation ──\n        if not self.batch_has_prefill:\n            # Decode: measure stalls from exec event gaps and barrier\n            # wait events recorded in V1 wrapper.\n            #\n            # Exec intervals span [begin_exec → end_exec] per graph\n            # piece.  They include the KV barrier wait (exec_attn_barriers\n            # wait in _after_replay) which delays attention start.\n            #\n            # The KV barrier wait is NOT caused by slow KV loading — it's\n            # caused by the weight→KV dependency chain: load_kv_stream\n            # waits for load_weight_stream, so the barrier is delayed.\n            #\n            # We report a single TotalStall = total_time - pure_exec.\n            # Th